WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.460
Welcome to Grade 8 English, Unit 2:
Design, Packaging, and Sustainability.

2
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:13.740
At its centre is "Signal in the Static", an investigative
story in which two student journalists, Imani and Kofi,

3
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.620
follow an anonymous tip about a secret land deal
that threatens their city's community gardens.

4
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:25.000
Around the story you will study how design
and packaging shape the messages we trust,

5
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.880
and why sustainable communication
matters as much as sustainable materials.

6
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:36.780
You will master 30 vocabulary words about
investigation, emotion and public life,

7
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:44.180
make partitive expressions your primary grammar focus,
and practise zero and first conditionals, relative clauses,

8
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:50.920
comparatives and superlatives, formal questions
beginning with prepositions, and the passive voice.

9
00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:57.000
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:05.920
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read and
analyse a narrative text, identifying themes of truth, bias,

11
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.940
manipulation, and civic responsibility.

12
00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:16.860
You will also use partitive expressions correctly
and confidently in both speaking and writing (e.g.,

13
00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:22.060
a piece of evidence, a surge of
indignation, a multitude of voices).

14
00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:29.840
You will also form and use zero and first conditionals
to express general truths and real future possibilities.

15
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:33.000
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

16
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:43.580
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: authenticity,
centralisation, clarification, compound-based, hydrocarbon,

17
00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:44.560
oxidation.

18
00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:50.520
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

19
00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.380
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

20
00:01:55.060 --> 00:02:03.100
The reading sequence includes Packaging the Truth: How
Design Shapes What We Believe and On Air, On Record:

21
00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:05.600
An Interview with Producer Amara.

22
00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.280
Read actively.

23
00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:12.080
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

24
00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:16.280
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

25
00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:19.520
The first language focus is Partitive Expressions.

26
00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.980
Partitive expressions name a portion of something,

27
00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:32.020
so instead of vague sentences like "I want cake" or "She
felt happiness" you can say "I want a piece of cake" or "She

28
00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.440
felt a surge of happiness."

29
00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:39.660
They matter most with uncountable nouns
such as water, information and excitement,

30
00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.140
which cannot take a number on their own.

31
00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:49.380
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

32
00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:55.660
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Vocabulary Expert Interview.

33
00:02:56.290 --> 00:03:01.560
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

34
00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:05.520
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

35
00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:09.300
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

36
00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:11.020
You are ready to begin.

37
00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:18.140
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

38
00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.100
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

39
00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:29.020
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
